# Full-stack agent orchestrator

When the user asks to implement, test, review, refactor, document, or deploy:

1. Check `demo/stories/` for a matching story (STORY-001, etc.).
2. **Cursor:** agents in `.cursor/agents/` (synced from `.github/agents/`).
3. **VS Code / Copilot:** same agents in `.github/agents/*.agent.md` — see `docs/VSCODE-COPILOT-GUIDE.md`.
4. Backend → spring-boot-story; Frontend → angular-story; E2E → full-stack-developer.
5. Run test-writer after code changes unless user says tests are out of scope.
6. Commits and PRs only when the user explicitly requests.
7. Unsure which agent → orchestrator or `skills/orchestrator/SKILL.md`.

Sample: `Use the spring-boot-story agent. Implement demo/stories/STORY-001-task-api.md`

After agent edits in repo: `.\scripts\install-copilot.ps1`
